{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions","id":986722,"title":"potential new setting questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-13T06:35:17-07:00","id":986722,"title":"potential new setting questions","content":"I am trying to figure out the side effects and ramifications of a setting where the masquerade has either worn thin or completely been destroyed. and if possible some ideas or flavour relating to such a setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/850-koolzombiez","name":"koolzombiez","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:43:11-07:00","id":986724,"title":"","content":"Well, it probably necessitates vampires being even more careful and paranoid. It probably also means a lot of Witch Hunts. Vampires will have to rely on their Disciplines a lot more to not get found out. Some will try to make it &quot;public&quot; but especially if the Masquerade's been lifted <i>recently</i> they'll run afoul of some terrible humans.<br /> <br /> Also, check out <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/82477/World-of-Darkness-Mirrors\" target=\"_blank\">World of Darkness: Mirrors</a> for World of Darkness Revealed, a setting hack that assumes the Masquerade isn't in effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T09:14:00-07:00","id":986798,"title":"","content":"That's the basic premise of the campaign I'm finishing. Most vampires were then hunted, captured and put inside a city-sized enclosure closed by a big big wall with a no man's land behind it and then massive Task Force Valkyrie presence, ready to nuke the place if things get out of hand. The vampires were sent building material bought with the Invictus' confiscated wealth and they receive neutered cows for feeding. A city was built to replace the tents and tunnels and the city now makes money with its cheap workforce (no health or retirement plan or feeding needed, they don't get tired and they can be much stronger and resilient than humans). It was pretty fun trying to think of as many elements as possible (like how many cows are needed, how much space they need and how that space can be optimised). Some rules needed to be tweaked too (daeva and nosferatu banes are moot).<br /> <br /> For one, I ruled that the &quot;vampires don't appear on photographs&quot; thing is a reflection of mortals being sort of unwilling to recognize the supernatural, so now the masquerade is dead, that's not a thing anymore, so they started making TV. Practical effects for blood and gore are a lot cheaper when all you need is a few liters of blood to regenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:43:17-07:00","id":986865,"title":"","content":"What about the vampires who can't feed on animals? The banes aren't moot as if they get out of this city, they could still feed on / interact with humans. <br /> <br /> I have also recently started a game where the Masquerade has been lifted. though it hasnt devolved into concentration camps...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:04:46-07:00","id":986876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=986865#post986865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the vampires who can't feed on animals? The banes aren't moot as if they get out of this city, they could still feed on / interact with humans.<br /> <br /> I have also recently started a game where the Masquerade has been lifted. though it hasnt devolved into concentration camps...</div> </div> </div> </div>They can always still feed on other vampires...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:08:37-07:00","id":986908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=986876#post986876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can always still feed on other vampires...</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. That is a setting problem or an interesting plot hook. Suddenly all these vampires are addicts, which most addicts have a gateway to the next. Which I see being diablerie as a next step in that. No greater rush. But suddenly you have a bunch of cracked out vampires with a need for vitae and there isnt enough to give it. the Animal eating vampires will have to feed more to keep up. the animals will be hurt more if there was only &quot;the right amount&quot; <br /> <br /> more frenzies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:38:40-07:00","id":986926,"title":"","content":"They don't get out, the entire campaign took place in the city. There's no real way out, the city is constantly being watched by drones that will shoot smartasses trying to fly over the walls. Then, once they're out, they need to go somewhere. The city was built in Kazakhstan, there's very very little feeding place in waking range, except from the Task Force Valkyrie camps, and they're looking out. Technically, it's possible to get out with the right set of disciplines and a good blood pool, but the odds are seriously not good.<br /> <br /> Really powerful vampires sometimes escaped capture and are hiding. The rest are encouraged to just go to sleep for a few decades. There's a ministry that takes care of a massive building with more than a million concrete boxes just for that. Most of the city is BP 1 to 3 (I ruled BP3 means you need twice as much animal blood and it stps being manageable at BP4). Feeding on other vampires is tolerated, and there are vampires who basically become prostitutes, getting paid to give their blood in sort of brothel-like establishments. Patrons usually try not to feed from the same vampire more than once.<br /> <br /> Then, there are the more problematic cases, like a Kingpin who owned a Casino. The casino clients who lost their money had the option, once, to ask for more chips, on the condition that they let the owner feed from them. It's technically legal because they didn't press charges. Some of the other high BP vampires can have mini cults, vassals, or some go as far as to prey on other vampires, they're rare, though.<br /> <br /> And then, there's the government. Some are low BP, but the Prince and some others get special privileges. Human blood pouches provided by the the humans, because a happy government is a stable government and a stable government keeps the business going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:05:56-07:00","id":986941,"title":"","content":"See, what I think would actually happen is:<br /> <br /> =&gt;Vampires turn on each other<br /> <br /> =&gt;Mass Diablerie<br /> <br /> =&gt; Blood Potency 10 victors punch down the wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:13:02-07:00","id":986946,"title":"","content":"That's one possibility, but then, there would be no game. Plus, by that time TFV would probably be ready to carpet bomb the place. Anyway, whoever would get out of there in one piece would be a draugr. A draugr ready to fall in torpor when it's big but limited blood pool quikcly runs out in a desert, in a world where most vampires have been caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:32:11-07:00","id":986956,"title":"","content":"Yeah, maybe. <br /> <br /> What happened to the Strix in this scenario?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:55:43-07:00","id":986966,"title":"","content":"They weren't as prominent as in 2ed, more like the mysterious threat from 1ed. Most people didn't know them, very few people had met some. They could be see sometimes, perched on the walls, watching. There's one that was pretty important though, Nameless from Montreal. It was a strix possessing a vampire and posing as a recluse elder ruling a small district and basically a strix invasion hazard. The specifics are complex and was part of a storyline involving a coup and a risk of civil war (which the players had to try and stop).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:22:24-07:00","id":987225,"title":"","content":"I agree that the vampires would turn on each other, Mass diablerie because they would be addicts and it would snow ball fast. Also. how would they contain vampires with Obfuscate. Or ones that can turn into animals? Or mist? Or vampires with Possession...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:48:00-07:00","id":987231,"title":"","content":"Mirrors: The World of Darkness Revealed Shard kind of touches on this subject a bit, on what happens when the Masquerade starts going down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:03:54-07:00","id":987427,"title":"","content":"The &quot;they would turn on each other because they would all be addicts&quot; is a matter of GM choice. Nothing easier than to rule vampires are smart enough to realize this would end badly for everybody, most likely including themselves.<br /> <br /> Depends if automated drones are affected by obfuscate. Possession is only useful if there's someone to possess. Animals at night are targets of drones too. And mist can be a solution if they can fly in mist form even then, there's still the problem of what to do once you're outside the walls. It's not much use being free if you're in a deserted area and the closest settlement is a Task Force Valkyrie camp with operatives ready to shoot on site or quarantine anybody suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:31:45-07:00","id":987487,"title":"","content":"Starving people can be desperate. Starving vampires moreso. Rational decision making tends to fall by the wayside in situations of extreme privation.<br /> <br /> Vampires who need human blood to survive only have kindred to feed on, so they're <i>going to be addicted</i>. It's inevitable, assuming they don't end up destroyed by whomever they try to feed on. The ones weak enough to feed on animals <i>might</i> do okay if there are enough animals to feed on, which strikes me as particularly doubtful. The most powerful elders would be in the best position, perhaps, since they're not subject to vitae addiction.<br /> <br /> So you have a very large segment of the vampire population addicted to vitae. What's the most likely thing to happen? It's not that everyone's going to settle down and be good neighbors to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:52:22-07:00","id":987493,"title":"","content":"The true blood route is also an option. A synthetic solution may have been found, or is in the works. <br /> <br /> If you keep out all the other supernatural fluff it's a pretty interesting concept. <br /> <br /> Religious zealots wanting to destroy them, the hunter population would be much larger. <br /> <br /> Whole PR campaigns to keep things covered up.<br /> <br /> I mean kindred would hold a lot of monetary sway. Locking them all up would cause a financial and societal collapse due to the power vacuum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:55:03-07:00","id":987494,"title":"","content":"Actually, there's a thing in the classic World of Darkness that is not entirely dissimilar to what you're doing.<br /> <br /> The Cappadocian clan founder locked up all of the Cappadocians who didn't meet his standards in an underground city. They basically diablerized each other until everyone who was left fell into torpor from starvation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:09:25-07:00","id":987497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>koolzombiez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions#post986722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying to figure out the side effects and ramifications of a setting where the masquerade has either worn thin or completely been destroyed. and if possible some ideas or flavour relating to such a setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was watching a live play session that followed the story of vampires acting in full view of the public. The governments of the world begrudgingly accepted them, but they had some conditions in place. One of which included the formation of a brand new security force specifically designed to keep vampires under control (kind of like True Blood's Authority).<br /> <br /> Also, thanks to some vampires going backwards in time and working some kind of mystical ritual, they could now walk in sunlight. I don't know the specifics, because they didn't go into great detail about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course when the world was made aware that immortal, super powered predators walked among them, this gave rise to new complications. One of which included vampire hate groups who operated a lot like the KKK, organizing into rallies dedicated to wiping out kindred establishments. The game focused less on political machinations, and more on social prejudice. The vampires were trying to manage their unlives while facing the struggles of human bigotry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-14-2016, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T00:49:21-07:00","id":987663,"title":"","content":"That's what the ministry of sleep and it's Mausoleum are there for. Obviously, there is also a police force controlled by the ministry of interior, as well as a prison (vampires in there are only fed in their private cell by a small tap before sunrise in so they can rise the next night so they are bloodless for most of the time, and falling into voluntary torpor only suspends your time, you get back in there when you wake up, diablerie is common in the prison, but those who become specialists of it usually keep doing it and don't come out at all). The vast majority of vampires are BP 1 to 3 (with the feeding scale being pushed back on rank) and the rest either have special privilege or are criminals. Feeding on another vampire is not technically illegal, although it is frowned upon (like in many domains where powerful vampires will sometimes go to sleep in order to avoid a disaster), but assaulting another for blood is. There is always disciplines to hide that, but one way or another, people notice when they're missing vitae and liberal use of disciplines like dominate is obviously mostly illegal. Obviously, if the vampires collectively decide to fuck shit up, it is going go collapse, but i's not like the only thing refraining them is their being reasonable.<br /> <br /> Most vampires also spend about 15 minutes doing a routine every night after waking up. It involves a composure+one skill the character has above 3 and is a sort of meditation. Some do katas, most do more mundane things like yoga exercises, reciting a content from a medical treaty, etc. Not doing it causes a small penalty on frenzy rolls because the setting is just bad for vampire minds There are stickers and posters in public places that read stuff like &quot;Have you done your waking routine ? It is important for you to keep a clear mind at all times.&quot;<br /> <br /> Look, at some point, I asked myself : Do I want to give my players a noir cyberpunk game in a prison City-State with only vampires. My answer was fuck yes. The next question was how could I somehow justify that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T02:36:35-07:00","id":987684,"title":"","content":"I guess the problem is that I don't see what prevents the vampires from being in constant frenzy from hunger and constantly out of willpower due to lack of opportunity to indulge mask and dirge. I don't see how such a situation is remotely sustainable for any length of time. I also don't see how any agency could establish such a perfect panopticon as you describe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-15-2016, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T03:38:07-07:00","id":987695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=987663#post987663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeding on another vampire is not technically illegal, although it is frowned upon (like in many domains where powerful vampires will sometimes go to sleep in order to avoid a disaster), but assaulting another for blood is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that someone who breaks this rule will be well-fed, while those who are trying to enforce it will not be, I don't really think this will matter. At all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T03:44:14-07:00","id":987697,"title":"","content":"They get willpower from sleeping. It's how it was in 1ed if I remember, and I liked it just fine. Dirge and Mask are also fine as long as they're not &quot;I'm a complete monster and I get my kicks from beating people up&quot;. I just consider the majority of active vampires in the world are relatively recent, twenty years or less so they're mostly regular humans who are still getting used to what they are. A good number never asked for any of this and just want to be left alone.<br /> <br /> I don't see why they'd have to frenzy all the time. They are fed. Animal blood, but they are fed and they usually try not to do stupid things and use their powers which would lead to them running out of vitae and becoming starved. They're rarely maxed out, but also rarely at a dangerous level. There's basically a system of ID linked food coupons. Everyone has the right to an amount of vitae that's enough to wake up and regenerate the occasional wound because they hit their small toe in the door frame. Getting more means having a job which gives you a certain amount per month that you can go &quot;collect&quot; in the various farms. I mean, yeah, vampires are violent creatures, but they're not irrational, and most don't want to die, so they rarely go out of their way to do things that will make them starve. They're also aware their neighbours are just as dangerous as they are and there are things they shouldn't do unless they want to risk dying. Add to that a government that's close to a police state. Add to that the various philosophies. The Invictus likes to have a feudal system and a well organized society, and people starving and frenzying left and right would end up making for a pretty lonely rule. The Lancea Sanctum is split and generally depressed, but it's still pretty against killing other kindred in general so they tend to insist on that when they can. The Carthians, I guess it depends on how you interpret them, but they want a working society, and while the Circle could find it fun to have a giant frenzy party, they also want to get out eventually, so everyone dying would not make it easier. Obviously, it's not sustainable very long term, it would probably collapse before it lasts a hundred years, probably even fifty, but the campaign will be over before that.<br /> <br /> Finally, maybe I'm nicer with frenzy rules than most GMs. I don't ask for frenzy rolls very often. Mostly, it's when the players just spent a lot of blood and go to refill at a farm. They start drinking the cow's blood, roll, fail, then couple guards jump on them and hold them on the ground until they calm down (one PC is getting a reputation for that now). I don't generally ask for an anger frenzy roll unless it's really personal, and fear frenzy is mostly fire and sunlight, and predictably, they tend not to see a whole lot of those. One PC had a fear frenzy when they went to a Circle ceremony and someone busted out a torch to test the crowd's spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T04:55:15-07:00","id":987707,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't get willpower from sleeping in second edition.<br /> <br /> And yes, you are extremely nice with frenzy rules.<br /> <br /> Also, vampires are not 100% pragmatic actors who only act rationally in their own best interests whenever they act at all. They have the Beast, and it drives them to do things they'll regret later, assuming they survive the experience. Heck, <i>humans</i> aren't 100% pragmatic actors who only act rationally in their own best interests, and vampires are just plain worse at it. Your ideas about what members of each covenant might <i>want</i> is very nice and all, but that doesn't mean they're going to <i>get</i> it. No one's going to be like &quot;Hey, let's all have a frenzy party and kill each other.&quot; It's just going to happen because this is what happens when you put vampires under stress - they frenzy. And a prison city full of vampires is a bomb ready to explode at any moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-15-2016, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T05:42:33-07:00","id":987710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=987707#post987707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't get willpower from sleeping in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> It should be noted that this never made it into the book nor is in the errata, so this isn't an official rule. Yes, the developers intended to put it in, but it slipped through the cracks. Death of the author, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T06:58:43-07:00","id":987728,"title":"","content":"I see the numerous flaws on the setting, but no reason to point them out, since the end is the setting itself. By myself, I would play it gladly, but mainly to figure a way out. That would be fun.<br /> <br /> On my take on the proposition, things had a lot of ramifications, but changed less than most people maybe think. Mortal society was shocked and confused at first, it was a great turmoil. But to be frank, mortal society is already in turmoil because of religion, sexuality, politics, economy, migration, etc.. Sooner or later it will get used and adapt, with extremists to both sides in the middle, as it get used to everything else in some way.<br /> <br /> So, in my game it was pure confusion for a couple of years until the first workable laws to deal with the vampires were issued. As a rule of thumb vampires were granted full civil rights in most countries, with some metaphysical discussions on the meaning of life in the meanwhile. As a rule, more severe actions against vampires were doomed by extreme costs and total ineffectivenes. A lot of vampires went hiding anyway for ease of unlife, and so most things actualy changed very little.<br /> <br /> Hunters didn't had that great time for long on most places. Even if knowing, most people don't have the strength of purpose to risk life against such creatures, so they numbered almost the same. It is also easier to voice against this to your authorities than to take things in one's own hands, so for each potential hunter that took to the Vigil because of the sudden knowledge, other actual hunter stepped down because didn't saw it as necessary anymore.<br /> <br /> A lot of hunters became members of actual official and well known special forces to take care of supernatural threats, and the old Conspiracies actualy took a harder blow for their methods whyle being substituted by more adapted ones (both legal and illegal). Curiously, as many as hunters, vampires and other supernatural things comprised the numbers of such forces, being as they are, the most apt to deal with criminals of their kinds. Other supernatural phenomena, not necessarily other splats, soon got out in the light since the first did it, as it became more easy to suspect, reason and accept such things now.<br /> <br /> The entire thing was fun, and very interesting. I'll probably run this again, but the most interesting for me was how much it <u>didn't</u> changed all that, but simply lessened the Masquerade focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:44:32-07:00","id":987800,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a fun setting. It's actually reasonnably close to how things get in one of the possibles campaigns of Gehenna from Masquerade. Vampires were caught on camera fighting an abomination in New York and the masquerade was blown. It's a reasonnably peaceful situation and the existence of vampires is generally well accepted and governments are like &quot;well, might as well do with those guys now&quot;. Then, things end badly... or well, depending on your point of view, but vampires end up disappearing because that's the theme of the book. The other scenario where the masquerade falls quickly escalates into a world war where humans panic and just try to eradicate vampires, then the old vampire gods wake up and use the earth as their personal pro wrestling ring. Then, vampires disappear and if the characters are lucky, they can maybe continue playing in a Mad Max-like world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 10-15-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:10:33-07:00","id":988028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=987684#post987684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the problem is that I don't see what prevents the vampires from being in constant frenzy from hunger and constantly out of willpower due to lack of opportunity to indulge mask and dirge. I don't see how such a situation is remotely sustainable for any length of time. I also don't see how any agency could establish such a perfect panopticon as you describe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> True. It's basically a case of the government rounding up as many vampires as possible, locking them up together and keeping them on the brink of starvation.<br /> <br /> YES, surely that will maintain peace and stability for generations to come! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Also, it says the government confiscated the Invictus' funding. I'm curious as to how they managed to do that. And I'm even more curious to know how they managed to round up the Lancea, Circle, and Dracul who couldn't give two shits about playing nice with humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> How do you capture a member of the Ordo Dracul when they've become resistant to standard capture methods? And they need less blood than normal to remain active, which means more blood they could be using to fuel their powers. I think one of their coils allows you to awaken for an entire week with just 1 point of Vitae.<br /> <br /> <br /> How do you control the Circle of the Crone, when they can perform a joint ritual to unleash any number of grisly effects upon the government's chain of command?<br /> <br /> <br /> How do you control the Lancea who believe it is their holy mandate to act like Satan, and have the power to invoke biblical curses upon their enemies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-15-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T22:09:32-07:00","id":988132,"title":"","content":"Biggest change, more house fires as keeping an open flame about becomes popular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:54:17-07:00","id":988175,"title":"","content":"But that's fine, they would just frenzy and kill each other because they're &quot;starving&quot;. Look, there are times as a GM, where the potential stories you can get from a setting/scenario far outweigh the few tweaks and theoretical inconsistencies the premises cause. Besides, vampires wouldn't &quot;actually&quot; turn on each other, vampires don't exist, they can't actually do anything, we like playing them because they're an extreme representation of some of our own aspects as human beings. None of my players had any problem with the basic premises of the setting and we had a pretty good time playing in it. I'd thought I'd just share something I worked on and had fun with, so I don't see the point in continually jumping on it to nitpick the very same point over and over.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, for like the fourth time, they're not starved. For those vampires who &quot;don't care to be nice to humans&quot;, chances are they just got killed or sent into torpor through damage. Task Force Valkyrie never expected everyone to turn themselves in anyway. Many vampires were destroyed at the time. A few really powerful ones escaped capture, most not so powerful ones could be captured, turned themselves in so they wouldn't be hunted, were shot/beaten to torpor and woke up inside the city. A bunch of mid range BP with enough power to think they could just escape easily and enough ego to try fought back or ran away for a while, generally to end up getting destroyed eventually.<br /> <br /> Nobody expected the masquerade to go down so quickly, so nobody really had time to prepare. Some descriptions of the Invictus have it sort of hide in plain sight, so they didn't have their money in fifteen different banks, through five fake societies. The human governments relatively quickly identified the companies that were controlled by the Invictus, and seized a share.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul did give some problems, and their goals were soon known of the hunter orgs. For this reason, one of the rules the humans imposed on the city's government was that they had to outlaw the Ordo Dracul. Since it's the smallest covenant, and the others had no particular problem with that, Ordo Practice was banned. What that means is that you can't open an official Ordo Dracul lab in the City. Those who learned coils could keep them, but not be caught studying more or doing scales. A bunch of them became underground scientists for hire, and of course, the government has a secret program and keeps a number of Ordo Researchers who can keep working in exchange for their security.<br /> <br /> The good thing about controling the Circle and the Lancea is that that they hate each other, so they're generally more busy mutually pointing fingers than working to topple the government and replace it with an entity that wouldn't last a week since it'd be a minority in the city. Their higher ups, the bishops, arch-bishops, cardinals, the high priestesses and priests have ties to the government. Some of the ministers are Lancea or Circle. The current government is composed of one Prince and twelve ministers, almost all of which belong to a covenant or have sympathies to that covenant. They managed to hit a balance point. The more hardline members of each covenant consider them traitors to be dealing with the enemies like that, but most realize that at least, that way, there is someone to negociate the humans sending cows so people don't starve. The Prince is pretty good at throwing everyone a bone to keep them satisfied enough that they won't go on a rampage.<br /> <br /> The Lancea and the Circle could do rituals to mess with the government, and some did, but that has the risk of being identified because of the blood sympathy it creates, it takes effort in a city where you don't want to waste vitae (and you can't just go murder clubbing to refill your willpower). Plus, and that's important. The covenants aren't monolithic entities. They generally have a tendency to dislike their traditional rivals, but a Circle cult who thinks they're being smart by fucking with the government with rituals has a pretty good chance to have other Circle members who'd rather not start a civil war come and kick them in the teeth or call the police.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum, for example, is very split. Basically, since they're locked up, they can't accomplish anything pertaining to their mission. Interpretations of their situation vary. Some see this as an obstacle to their mission and that they have to survive while looking for a way out, some figure they've failed somehow and this is their punishment, so they'll just have to take it until god decides to release them, some other figure that the reason they failed and were punished was because they didn't understand Longinus' message and so they need to go back to the drawing board and potentially come up with a new interpretation of the testament. Finally, there are those few who think that they have to keep straightening humanity, except if they can't do it directly, they'll have to show how monstrous they can be, so their plan is to cause as much chaos in the city so that everyone will either kill each other or the military will decide to nuke them.<br /> <br /> The Circle has different views altogether, and it's even less of a coherent group from the start. I really like how they encourage creation and attract artists within kindred. A certain number of them, while wishing they could just get out, think this is actually a fascinating opportunity. Vampires are, at last, completely cut from humanity and only have each other to draw inspiration from. They're hoping that a form of society, expression and art uniquely kindred will emerge from what they see as sort of a giant crucible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T22:27:27-07:00","id":989213,"title":"","content":"Most of those seem reasonable enough, except for banning the Ordo Dracul, who are possibly their best chance to escape their new living conditions. Coils that allow them to remain functional with significantly less vitae than normal, as well as better maintain control of their Beast and resist (though still susceptible to) the weaknesses that plague other vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> But no, we can forget all that good stuff, because everybody knows that if there's one thing vampires love, it's being in a position of weakness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Even if the vampires can't openly practice such things, there doesn't seem to be anything stopping them from doing it behind closed doors. It sounds like the city is populated entirely by vampires, or else they wouldn't need to send in cows if there's a human presence involved. In order to enforce this law, the government would either need to send patrols inside the city (where they are vulnerable to attack), or just bomb the place outright and waste the billions of dollars they spent building the prison in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> My take on the scenario is that many of the disenfranchised or unbound kindred would be flocking to the Ordo Dracul in the hopes of aiding their research, enabling them to allocate more funds and energy towards perfecting the vampire condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> You've said that the majority of the city is populated by BP 1-3 vampires. These, however, are buck neonates when you consider that BP goes all the way up to 10. Blood Potency 3 isn't even half of their full potential.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically, the government rounded up all the weaklings who couldn't fend for themselves, while the <i>real threats</i> are still out there somewhere.<br /> <br /> Remember that Vigor, Celerity and Resilience are basic powers that nearly any vampire can learn easily, and those push their physical prowess well beyond <i>maximum human limits</i>. But add to that the fact that they also have mystical disciplines which give them powers that defy scientific explanation, and it becomes much less believable that they remain docile so easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-18-2016, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T02:08:46-07:00","id":989259,"title":"","content":"Yeah, It would go something like<br /> <br /> Humans: &quot;Ordo Dracul Membership is banned&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampires: &quot;OK.&quot; *Literally everyone joins the Ordo Dracul*<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not like their practices were legal <i>before...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-18-2016, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T03:10:08-07:00","id":989271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=989213#post989213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But no, we can forget all that good stuff, because everybody knows that if there's one thing vampires love, it's being in a position of weakness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, and being completely honest with people about what they're up to. Yep, kindred have never lied about their plans or nightly activities. <i>Not to each other, and certainly never to kine!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:07:20-07:00","id":989378,"title":"","content":"While I think this is a great short term thing. I am with the others that this would not be sustainable. I do believe that most vampires wouldn't last caged up like that. You say they arent starving, but they only have exactly the right amount to feed on... So when they dont ration it out properly, which they wouldnt, they would become starving rather quickly. Vampires need it to wake, use powers, have sex, whatever. There is no way to figure out &quot;the right amount&quot; because they burn it at different paces for different things.<br /> <br /> The thing with the lance, the crone and whatever else not working together... I guarantee if England started bombing the US and Russia.. we would team up and take them down if it was a real threat.. A common enemy brings enemies together. even if it is only for a short time and to try and fuck over the other in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:45:47-07:00","id":989738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=989378#post989378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I think this is a great short term thing. I am with the others that this would not be sustainable. I do believe that most vampires wouldn't last caged up like that. You say they arent starving, but they only have exactly the right amount to feed on... So when they dont ration it out properly, which they wouldnt, they would become starving rather quickly. Vampires need it to wake, use powers, have sex, whatever. There is no way to figure out &quot;the right amount&quot; because they burn it at different paces for different things.<br /> <br /> The thing with the lance, the crone and whatever else not working together... I guarantee if England started bombing the US and Russia.. we would team up and take them down if it was a real threat.. A common enemy brings enemies together. even if it is only for a short time and to try and fuck over the other in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Adding to that there are other covenants who are flat out impossible to control. The Seven, for example, want to exterminate vampires for whatever crazy reason has them all brainwashed. It doesn't matter if it's over blood or not. You round a bunch of them up in a vampire city and there's going to be mayhem in the streets. And then, of course, there's Belial's Brood who are a gigantic, blood smeared <b>&quot;Fuck No!&quot;</b> on this entire premise.<br /> <br /> From what they've said, it sounds like the masquerade being blown wasn't a desired outcome. It was accidental and most vampires weren't prepared for it. Nothing we know about vampires would indicate they up and decide &quot;well, cover's blown. Time to play nice.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Vitalis is right, this premise, while intriguing, is not sustainable. At best, it could serve as a <i>prequel </i>to another setting in which mortals and kindred are engaged in open warfare with each other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-19-2016, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T03:17:43-07:00","id":989811,"title":"","content":"It's not supposed to be sustainable indefinitely. The purpose is to eradicate the vampire population. Once they're gone, operation was a success, move on to the next undesirable supernatural slated for extermination.<br /> <br /> Seven would be the collaborators who are given special privileges for cooperating (the last ones to be exterminated) or placed in police units to track down and slaughter the vampires the governments couldn't catch (Belial's Brood) or escaped. Or the pet lapdog of a politico who uses a vampire assassin to eliminate obstructions to their ambitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 10-19-2016, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T03:31:19-07:00","id":989813,"title":"","content":"So, in other words, after a slight hiccup the vampires would throw a bunch of neonates under a bus and then continue pretty much as they always have done, with mortals thinking they don't exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T06:06:02-07:00","id":989840,"title":"","content":"Another thing about the strix. They're not particularly working on fucking with vampires so far since they're pretty pleased with the situation so far and having a laugh at them trapped like rats. They also now have the entire earth to play with and make a mess in. A few like to look at the city from the wall. Another bad surprise for the vampire who decides to fly away by turning into a bat and escapes the drones.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't have the calculations on me, but I think I set it up so the number of cows is more or less enough to get every vampire an average of 2 to 3 vitae a day. The distribution is less than that usually because since they cows they get are neutered, they want to keep them alive as long as possible and not strain them too much, but there's the possibility (at least unless the kindred scientists manage to clone them reliably enough).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=989378#post989378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with the lance, the crone and whatever else not working together... I guarantee if England started bombing the US and Russia.. we would team up and take them down if it was a real threat.. A common enemy brings enemies together. even if it is only for a short time and to try and fuck over the other in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't know about that. The most durable and violent hatred in history have usually been between culturally close civilizations. When a bigger potential invader comes, it's not unusual for one of those civilizations to strike an alliance with the new power, not realizing they're playing into the invader's hand and making their job easier in the long run.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Lancea and Circle don't really have any ideolgical common ground they could agree on. Sure, a number of vampires would be ready to cooperate to get out, but for the fervent Lancea, siding with the circle would be comparable to working with demons. What I think is a superficial alliance would dwindle soon, once they realize they're not getting out anytime soon, and a more efficient alliance, while possible, would take much much longer to appear.<br /> <br /> I didn't include Belial's Brood in the setting because I didn't have any plan with it. I had planned to include 7 as the weird psychokinetic vampires from the 7 supplement, but in the end, I had more important stuff to focus on, so as far as the players are concerned, they've never heard of 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 10-19-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:19:32-07:00","id":989886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=989840#post989840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus, the Lancea and Circle don't really have any ideolgical common ground they could agree on. Sure, a number of vampires would be ready to cooperate to get out, but for the fervent Lancea, siding with the circle would be comparable to working with demons. What I think is a superficial alliance would dwindle soon, once they realize they're not getting out anytime soon, and a more efficient alliance, while possible, would take much much longer to appear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Survival is common ground. Survival often trumps religious beliefs. The X and the Y are both going to work together if the government is hellbent on killing them both. they will duke it out when the stronger threat is over. And in times of dire problems. Sure they will call in the Z to help even if that Z is Demons. <br /> <br /> You asked us for help and several of us seem to think that this wouldn't last long... I think if the humans started a war like this, to eradicate all the vampires... the humans would lose. Vampires would be mass embracing and mind fucking over the human population. Not to mention that the Circle can kill people from a distance given a little time. How do you eradicate the Gangrel with protean who can just turn into a rat and scurry just about anywhere undetected. Vampires could survive in nuclear fallout. <br /> <br /> It would be a very interesting game to play in for sure, but it would not be a situation that would last years or decades.. It would be fast and bloody... especially if the other supernaturals realized.. once the vampires are gone.. what's to stop the humans from coming after them next? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:53:10-07:00","id":990116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=989811#post989811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not supposed to be sustainable indefinitely. The purpose is to eradicate the vampire population. Once they're gone, operation was a success, move on to the next undesirable supernatural slated for extermination.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the plan is to wipe them out, they're going about it in the stupidest fashion possible. Cities don't just pop into existence, they need somebody to build them. Those people need resources, which cost money, and those resources need maintenance, which requires more resources and more money. Maintaining a steady supply of <i>neutered cows</i> also requires money for resources, living arrangements, and also time so the cows can grow to maturity.<br /> <br /> Then, of course you have the high tech drones, which require maintenance and the TFV encampments which require resources to maintain a secure presence, as well as government pay checks to continue doing their jobs. I guarantee you, nobody is going to risk their ass in the middle of an empty desert guarding super powered monsters without demanding compensation.<br /> <br /> <br /> You know what method wipes out vampires faster and cheaper than maintaining a prison city?<br /> <br /> <b>Killing them on sight!</b><br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------<br /> <br /> But that's just the threat to the tax payers. The soldiers guarding them face a more immediate threat. Protean doesn't just let you turn into a bat or wolf, those are just the most common animals. A protean user can turn into any animal. What if a vampire manages to escape by turning into a mosquito and grabbing some TFV soldiers for a quick bite? Speaking from experience you don't feel every mosquito that bites you, at least not until after they're already gone and the bite starts itching. And by that point, you've got a freshly fed vampire who can pop in out of nowhere because they're so tiny.<br /> <br /> <br /> And those drones better be anti-vehicle models, or any vampire with Celerity is going to weave in and out of their machine gun fire. Also, vampires are more durable than humans. Bullets only inflict bashing damage to them, which means even if a stray bullet hits them, it's either just going to piss them off, or (if they have resilience) barely make them flinch as they charge through it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-19-2016, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T04:54:00-07:00","id":990370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=989886#post989886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You asked us for help and several of us seem to think that this wouldn't last long...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, wait, I never asked you for help. The person who created the threat did. I just answered his thread and mentioned the setting I played with. I do not need help with that setting, I built it extensively, with a map of the city with dozens of landmarks/places of interest, composition of the government and how it generally works, a bunch of NPCs, government, criminals regular inhabitants and other, background secrets. I set up a whole campaign based around that setting. I have played that campaign for over a year now and am one game close to finish it pretty much as I intended.<br /> <br /> So no, I do not need help coming up with that setting, I'm sorry for the confusion if I generated it. I understand your insistance better now, and you should understand your insistance is making me feel like you're telling me to stop having fun and that I've been playing vampire wrong because you would play it differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T05:14:17-07:00","id":990373,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> I mean, it was to be expected that there would be some debate regarding how accurate your campaign had been to canon characterisations, but it kind of took over the thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:37:45-07:00","id":990428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=990370#post990370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, wait, I never asked you for help. The person who created the threat did. I just answered his thread and mentioned the setting I played with. I do not need help with that setting, I built it extensively, with a map of the city with dozens of landmarks/places of interest, composition of the government and how it generally works, a bunch of NPCs, government, criminals regular inhabitants and other, background secrets. I set up a whole campaign based around that setting. I have played that campaign for over a year now and am one game close to finish it pretty much as I intended.<br /> <br /> So no, I do not need help coming up with that setting, I'm sorry for the confusion if I generated it. I understand your insistance better now, and you should understand your insistance is making me feel like you're telling me to stop having fun and that I've been playing vampire wrong because you would play it differently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright as Elfive pointed out that perhaps we all got a little side tracked about how accurately it would work. Of course when there is a thread called &quot;Potential new setting questions&quot; One just assumes that this is a QandA sort of thing. Questions come up and people have Answers. You opened up your setting for those Q&amp;A by trying to explain it, which made us all have more questions. which people had more answers to.. which brought more questions. Viscous Cycle.<br /> <br /> We are all glad that you had fun doing it. No one here is going to tell you to not have fun. No one here said to stop having fun. I said on multiple accounts that I thought that it would be a fun setting to explore, I just didnt think that it would be (Cannon wise) A lasting one.<br /> <br /> We all understand that everyone plays this game differently. Some people prefer to play it closer to cannon and some people just want to do what they want to do with as much homebrewery as can be. And there is no right or wrong way to play it. It's just what works for you and what doesn't. If that setting worked for you and your group and you all had a good time. Well then that's fantastic. No one wants to take that away from you or to tell you to stop doing it. All that some of us said was it wouldn't work for us.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: As a matter of Fact I am sure that you could all pretty much destroy my setting as it probably wouldn't work Cannonwise either. What had happen to smash the masquerade in the game, was that a Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling and a Mage in DC decided to make a public announcement of the existence of Supernaturals on National TV with the president on their side. <br /> <br /> Sure mages could go back in time and change that from happening, Or werewolves could erase any proof that ever happened. Why would a changeling expose themselves like that? So it would open up just as many questions and problems too... What we are doing is working through those problems. <br /> <br /> I took over that setting and sent the group into Wonderland or something similar...(Arcadia)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 10-20-2016, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:12:24-07:00","id":990501,"title":"","content":"That does sound like a fun campaign, and we had a similar session in a multi-splat game where a sensitive piece of information (that one of the players, playing a werewolf was the reincarnation of father wolf) got out. I pointed out of game to the GM that this would probably break the setting (which he didn't want) since there was no way that PC was going to be left alone and would have to contend with attempts to make him world alpha, to assassinate him, to discredit him, etc. So in the next game, we had to go to the Temenos (collective unconscious) to delete that information and retroactively undo what basically ended as a werewolf world war.<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't know, there are games that have a metaplot, written campaigns (my best roleplaying experience was as a player in a game with a set and very detailed background), and even mechanics that are so closely tied to the background touching anything messes with everything. I don't really consider that Requiem has a &quot;cannon&quot;. Sometimes I'm even annoyed at how Requiem books are on purpose, you never really know anything. The bright side is that with so little incentive, you can really do anything you want, and if an idea comes up, but a few rules get in a way of it, decide which is more important.<br /> <br /> I stand by the campaign I've built. I've had tremendous fun with it, both conceiving it (which involved discussions on how that would work) and GMing it and as far as I know, my players had a pretty good time too. There are countless settings where you could point out flaws and feel like it couldn't have come into existence. For what it's worth, the players didn't see any of this happening. Some of their characters did, but the campaign started 20 years into the setting with the city being established and functioning somewhat (full of resigned and depressed vampires) and the PCs getting recruited into a special task force by the vampire government to fight crime. While doing that, they would uncover little by little the true reason for the city's existence. In game, less than a year happened as they've been pretty active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:01:09-07:00","id":990669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=990373#post990373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> I mean, it was to be expected that there would be some debate regarding how accurate your campaign had been to canon characterisations, but it kind of took over the thread</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, crap, I just realized that, too. Man, we got distracted, didn't we? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, there are potentials on both sides of the setting for what would happen if the Masquerade were ever brought down. If vampires were willing to maintain a civilized code of conduct and treated mortals as actual people, then I could see a setting in which they are at the very least tolerated by mortals, if not accepted by them.<br /> <br /> In fact, going public about their existence might actually help them maintain their humanity, as it would remove the need to keep secrets about themselves from their touchstones who happen to be living beings. Not to mention modern media portraying vampires as something to be admired could prove beneficial if the vampire knows how to take advantage of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> If, however, the vampires still treated mortals as nothing more than food or pawns, then you also have the likely scenario of open warfare between the two species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-22-2016, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:30:34-07:00","id":990680,"title":"","content":"I can't help but picture the reaction of the general public as one lost masquerade triggers a chain reaction and more and more monsters just pour out of the shadows like some comical extended disarming sequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:56:40-07:00","id":990688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=990680#post990680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but picture the reaction of the general public as one lost masquerade triggers a chain reaction and more and more monsters just pour out of the shadows like some comical extended disarming sequence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kind of what happened in the game we were playing. Other supernaturals who wanted to help show the world they werent mosters were making youtube videos, facebook posts, or doing TV interviews or coming out as owning clubs or whatever. People started breaking it everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T22:42:16-07:00","id":991289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=990680#post990680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but picture the reaction of the general public as one lost masquerade triggers a chain reaction and more and more monsters just pour out of the shadows like some comical extended disarming sequence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That'd be kind of hard for werewolves, though.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, we're werewolves!&quot; <b>*shows off shapeshifting*</b><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Well that sounds- AAAHHH, holy shit!!&quot; <b>*lunacy kicks in*</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:39:27-07:00","id":991899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=991289#post991289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That'd be kind of hard for werewolves, though.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, we're werewolves!&quot; <b>*shows off shapeshifting*</b><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Well that sounds- AAAHHH, holy shit!!&quot; <b>*lunacy kicks in*</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Haha! Yeah we didnt have the werewolves show anything off due to that problem. I never thought about it until just now. Could you video a werewolf changing? I mean would it cause the Lunacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:49:23-07:00","id":991905,"title":"","content":"In 1e it would cause a modified version where the viewer would absolutely refuse to believe it was real. I don't know if anything official has been said about 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:56:54-07:00","id":991910,"title":"","content":"There's a nice rite that deletes videos and other recorded evidence of supernatural acts.<br /> <br /> But Elfive is right it's not been made clear. Based on the description I'd say yes, with a minor penalty. It would be incredibly easy to dismiss a YouTube video as, 'It's just special effects.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T22:55:53-07:00","id":994418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986722-potential-new-setting-questions?p=989886#post989886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Survival is common ground. Survival often trumps religious beliefs. The X and the Y are both going to work together if the government is hellbent on killing them both. they will duke it out when the stronger threat is over. And in times of dire problems. Sure they will call in the Z to help even if that Z is Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with this, with an added addendum; these vampires have one big thing in common; they're all enthusiastic blood junkies who will never again know the sweet taste of human juice until they somehow escape/bargain.<br /> <br /> You don't know terror until you've faced seventy superhuman dry drunks in lockstep grimly angling for a drink. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}